course: dictionary
lesson: 9936
title: Taproots and fibrous roots
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A plant's roots hold it in the ground and drink up water. A taproot is one large main root that grows straight down into the soil, with smaller roots growing off it. Read the clue in «a long taproot finds water deep down»: deep down tells you where the root goes.
explain: Scientists compare taproots with fibrous roots. Fibrous roots are many thin roots, like grass, and they stay near the surface. A taproot is one big root, and fibrous roots are lots of little ones.
explain: A taproot can do two jobs. It anchors the plant, and it reaches water far below. In carrots and beetroot it also stores food, which is why we eat them. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A taproot is a large main root that grows straight down into the ground.
fact: Smaller roots grow off the side of a taproot.
fact: Carrots, parsnips, radishes and dandelions have taproots.
fact: «A dandelion has a thick deep taproot that stores food.»
fact: Fibrous roots are many thin roots, like grass, while a taproot is one main root.
exercise: What is a taproot? | A leaf that grows underground | Many thin roots that spread out near the top of the soil | *A large main root that grows straight down into the ground | A flower that opens at night
exercise: Which of these plants has a taproot? | Grass | Wheat | Reeds | *Dandelion
exercise: «Grass has many thin fibrous roots near the surface.» What are fibrous roots? | *Many thin roots, like grass, near the surface | A stem covered in buds | One large root that grows straight down | Roots that only grow in water
test: Why does a taproot help a plant? | *It holds the plant firm and reaches water deep down | It makes the plant change colour | It lets the plant fly away on the wind | It makes the flowers open faster
test: Which food do we eat from a taproot? | *Beetroot | Cabbage leaf | Pea pod | Strawberry
exam: Using «a long taproot finds water deep down», what does a taproot probably do? | Grows fruit on the branches | Floats away on tiny parachutes | Turns the leaves red in autumn | *Reaches deep down for water
